# Land work on master

This repo lost a whole feature series because PRs were stacked (`base: previous-branch`) and only the first PR targeted `master`. GitHub showed MERGED; `master` never got the commits.

## Rules

- Default to **one PR targeting `master`**. Split only when the user asks, or a later PR cannot compile without an earlier one that is already merged.
- If you must stack, **retarget each remaining PR to `master` after the previous one merges**, rebase, and confirm `git merge-base --is-ancestor <merge-commit> origin/master`.
- Do not treat a PR as shipped because GitHub says MERGED. Check ancestry on `origin/master`.
- Never open PR 2 with `base: feat/pr1` unless the user explicitly wants a stack **and** you will retarget after merge.

```bash
# ❌ BAD — looks merged, never reaches master
gh pr create --base feat/hide-keys --head feat/families

# ✅ GOOD
gh pr create --base master --head feat/families
```
